// Faísca's sounds (islandPetSounds), off unless chosen. Each of 25 events has
// its own switch and its own source: the island's (synthesized here, with
// oscillators, envelopes, filters and a small room), a pack downloaded when
// chosen (kPetSoundPacks), or a file of the user's (.wav, .mp3...).
//
// Playing: PetPlaySound, from any thread, checks the cheap things first and
// queues a request. One audio thread (started by the first sound, ended
// after kPetSoundIdleMs of silence) makes or finds each sound's samples,
// mixes the ones playing and feeds a waveOut stream (winmm is already
// linked; XAudio2 would add a library, and WASAPI a thread of its own per
// stream). Files are read on a loader thread, so the mix never waits for
// the disk or for a decoder. Nothing runs, and nothing is kept in memory,
// while no sound plays.

